  "raw": {
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4ca93b73-7ad8-4b7e-9865-fba9ae4e8e47&ccId=9200344927168_2&jobId=9201450104271_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Instructional Designer and EdTech Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\n\nLocation: Berea\n\nDepartment:  Educational Technology /Academic Affairs Reports To:  Senior Associate Provost  Employment Type:  Full-Time FLSA Status:  Exempt Schedule:  Monday–Friday, 8:30 a.m.–5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement:  Remote work arrangements may be possible in accordance with University policy. On-site availability in Berea, OH, is preferred.   Job Summary  The Instructional Designer and Educational Technology Specialist partners with faculty and staff to enhance teaching and learning through effective instructional design, pedagogy, learning technologies, and emerging technologies. The position provides a hybrid of Learning Management System (LMS) support and strategic instructional design expertise, with particular emphasis on faculty development, course design, accessibility, Quality Matters standards, artificial intelligence (AI), and emerging educational technologies. The position provides functional support and administration for the University's Canvas LMS and selected educational technology applications while helping faculty move beyond the technical use of technology to its intentional and effective application to teaching and learning. The position consults with faculty on the design and delivery of online, hybrid, and HyFlex courses; provides professional development; supports responsible and effective use of AI and emerging technologies; and evaluates technologies for their pedagogical value. The successful candidate will bring strong knowledge of instructional design and the science of learning, current educational technology trends, and emerging technologies and will be able to translate those areas of expertise into practical support for faculty with varying levels of technological experience.   Position Emphasis  The position intentionally balances three complementary areas of responsibility: LMS and educational technology support  – ensuring faculty, staff, and students have reliable functional support for Canvas and University-supported technologies. Instructional design and faculty development  – partnering with faculty to strengthen course design, pedagogy, assessment, accessibility, and student engagement. Emerging technology and AI leadership  – helping the University and its faculty understand, evaluate, and responsibly integrate rapidly evolving technologies into teaching and learning. Essential Functions and Responsibilities  The following outlines the primary functions of the position and is not intended to be a complete description of all duties. LMS and Educational Technology Support  Provide functional support for the University's Canvas LMS for faculty, staff, and students, including navigation, course development, content organization, assignments, assessments, rubrics, modules, and other LMS features. Perform designated Canvas LMS administration, configuration, troubleshooting, third-party integrations, LTI management, and coordination with Information Technology and vendors. Assist with resolving educational technology issues and coordinate with the IT Help Desk and vendors when issues require additional technical support. Develop and maintain instructional resources, tutorials, documentation, and other materials that support effective use of the LMS and educational technologies. Instructional Design and Faculty Consultation  Partner with faculty to design and redesign effective, engaging, accessible, and student-centered courses and learning experiences. Advise faculty on instructional strategies, learning activities, assessment, course organization, student engagement, and alignment of learning outcomes with instructional methods. Provide specialized consultation for online, hybrid, and HyFlex course design and delivery. Apply principles of instructional design, science of learning, universal design for learning, accessibility, and effective pedagogy to course development. Conduct course reviews using Quality Matters (QM) standards and support faculty in identifying and implementing opportunities for course improvement. Provide consultation and technical support related to electronic promotion and tenure portfolios as needed. Faculty Development and Emerging Technologies  Develop and facilitate professional development opportunities for faculty and staff focused on instructional design, pedagogy, educational technology, AI, and emerging technologies. Provide individual and group consultations to help faculty identify appropriate technologies and determine how those technologies can enhance teaching and learning. Serve as a campus resource for AI in teaching and learning, including emerging AI tools, AI-aware course design, assessment strategies, academic integrity, accessibility, and responsible and ethical use. Monitor developments in AI and other emerging educational technologies and assess their potential instructional applications, limitations, risks, and benefits. Support faculty experimentation and innovation with emerging technologies through consultations, demonstrations, pilots, and professional learning. Evaluate educational technology tools for instructional effectiveness, accessibility, usability, integration, and alignment with institutional needs. Participate in professional conferences, workshops, seminars, communities of practice, and other learning opportunities to maintain current knowledge of instructional design, pedagogy, AI, and emerging educational technologies. Faculty and Employee Development  Provide onboarding and training for new faculty related to Canvas, instructional technologies, course design, and effective teaching practices. Support ongoing employee professional development related to educational technology, instructional design, pedagogy, AI, and emerging technologies. Develop workshops, presentations, videos, guides, and other professional learning resources responsive to faculty and staff needs. Collaborate with academic and administrative units to identify instructional technology and faculty development priorities. Collaboration and Institutional Support  Collaborate with Information Technology, Academic Affairs, faculty, staff, and other University partners to advance effective teaching and learning through technology. Serve as a liaison between faculty and Information Technology for instructional technology needs, helping translate pedagogical needs into appropriate technical solutions. Contribute to institutional initiatives involving online learning, educational technology, AI, accessibility, academic innovation, and student success. Participate in Quality Matters membership activities, course identification, reviews, and related quality-assurance initiatives. Maintain timely communication regarding projects, emerging issues, technology needs, and faculty support trends. Perform other duties as assigned by the Senior Associate Provost and/or Senior Instructional Designer. Qualifications  Required  Master's degree in Instructional Design, Instructional Technology, Educational Technology, Learning Design, eLearning, or a closely related field. Three or more years of professional experience in instructional design, educational technology, learning experience design, or a related field. Demonstrated experience designing and supporting online, hybrid, and/or HyFlex courses. Demonstrated experience supporting and administering Canvas or another major LMS. Strong knowledge of instructional design principles, learning science, effective pedagogy, assessment, accessibility, and student-centered course design. Demonstrated ability to provide faculty development and individualized consultation to faculty with varying levels of technological expertise. Demonstrated knowledge of current educational technologies and emerging technologies, including generative AI and its applications in teaching and learning. Ability to evaluate technology tools not only for technical functionality but also for pedagogical effectiveness, accessibility, usability, and instructional value. Strong interpersonal, written, verbal, presentation, and consultation skills. Ability to work collaboratively within an academic environment and establish effective relationships with faculty and staff. Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines. Ability to adapt, learn continuously, and remain current in a rapidly changing educational and technological environment. Preferred  Quality Matters certification or experience conducting QM course reviews. Experience with AI-enabled educational technologies and AI-aware teaching and learning practices. Experience with Universal Design for Learning and accessible course development. Experience with Canvas administration and third-party integrations/LTIs. Experience with video, lecture capture, multimedia, polling, collaboration, and presentation technologies. Experience developing instructional videos, tutorials, websites, infographics, and other digital learning resources. Experience with helpdesk or ticketing systems. Experience supporting faculty with electronic promotion and tenure portfolios. Experience working in higher education. Working Conditions and Physical Effort  Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office environment or from a dedicated home office. The position may require occasional movement to classrooms, offices, or other campus locations to support instructional technology, faculty development, and educational technology initiatives. The position requires the ability to sit, stand, hear, and see continuously, and to walk, write, and type frequently. Occasional lifting of up to 25 pounds may be required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of this position. How to Apply  Review of completed applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For strongest consideration, please submit your application before November 16, 2026 . Interested candidates should submit a resume and cover letter via the “To Apply” link on Baldwin Wallace University’s Employment and Careers webpage. We appreciate all applicants; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Additional Information  Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check, meeting applicable pre-employment requirements, and compliance with University and departmental policies, including completion of required training. Baldwin Wallace University is an EEO employer and educator. We provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees in accordance with applicable federal, state, and local laws. At BW, we support and encourage diversity in a variety of forms. We value and appreciate inclusive excellence in the classroom, within extracurricular activities and as we engage our community partners.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4ca93b73-7ad8-4b7e-9865-fba9ae4e8e47&ccId=9200344927168_2&jobId=9201450081040_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Starbucks Store Receiver - BW Campus",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\n\nLocation: Berea\n\nReports To: Store Manager Employment Type: Full-Time  FLSA Status: Non-Exempt  Position Summary  A BW Starbucks Store Receiver manages the daily operations of the back of house, including stockroom organization and cleanliness, inventory counts, and weekly ordering. This position requires strong administrative accuracy to handle tracking orders, checking deliveries, and planning weekly stock behind the scenes, while remaining a hands-on presence on the floor as a barista when needed. This is a full-time, non-exempt position at a Starbucks licensed coffeehouse on the Baldwin Wallace campus. Essential Duties & Responsibilities    Responsibilities may include, but are not limited to, the following:  Monitor store stock levels and use store software to place accurate, timely weekly orders for food, beverage, retail, and operational supplies. Meet delivery drivers, verify incoming physical stock against purchase orders/invoices, inspect product quality, and log any shorted or damaged items for management review. Prepare and process purchase orders while ensuring accuracy, obtaining appropriate approvals, and adhering to established purchasing procedures.  Verify all invoices against purchase orders, note discrepancies, and accurately maintain all receiving and purchasing documentation for supervisor review. Conduct weekly and monthly physical inventory counts and report differences between system stock and actual stock to management.  Keep the stockroom, refrigerators, and freezer neat, organized, clean, and properly labeled. Rotate all items using First-In, First-Out rules to prevent expiration and ensure local health department standards are met. Count and log daily product waste or broken items so the store can actively reduce unnecessary losses. Assist as barista when needed, helping craft beverages, serve customers, and keep lines moving. Position Requirements  Minimum Qualifications One year of operational or leadership experience within a hospitality, food and beverage or retail environment. Experience working with digital inventory systems, tracking product waste, and management cash/payment transactions on point-of-sale systems.  Strong verbal and written communication skills with a high degree of accuracy when auditing delivery invoices and submitting weekly stock orders. Ability to multi-task in a fast-paced environment. Highly responsible and able to maintain strict confidentiality.  Strong interpersonal skills, flexibility, and willingness to learn and build relationships. Preferred Qualifications  Experience with procurement and inventory management and control practices (such as FIFO rotation) is strongly preferred. Experience in a high-volume retail, food service, hospitality, distribution, or coffee shop environment, especially as a barista. Prior successful completion of ServSafe certification, barista training, and certification in beverage preparation standards and commercial beverage equipment operation, or ability to obtain certification within a specified training period. Working Conditions & Physical Requirements  Work is performed in a fast-paced retail environment requiring standing for extended periods and frequent walking, bending, twisting, and reaching. Must be able to lift, carry, and move items weighing up to 50 pounds. Work may involve exposure to confined spaces and high customer traffic. Shifts may include early mornings, evenings, weekends, nights, and holidays. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. Conditions of Employment  Must successfully pass a background check. Successful completion of ServSafe certification, barista training, and certification in beverage preparation standards and commercial beverage equipment operation, or ability to obtain certification within a specified training period.   How to Apply Review of completed applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates should submit a resume via the “To Apply” link on Baldwin Wallace University’s Employment and Careers webpage. We appreciate all applicants; only those selected for an interview will be contacted.  Additional Information Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check, meeting applicable pre-employment requirements, and compliance with University and departmental policies, including completion of required training.    Baldwin Wallace University is an EEO employer and educator. We provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees in accordance with applicable federal, state, and local laws. At BW, we support and encourage diversity in a variety of forms. We value and appreciate inclusive excellence in the classroom, within extracurricular activities and as we engage our community partners.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4ca93b73-7ad8-4b7e-9865-fba9ae4e8e47&ccId=9200344927168_2&jobId=9201437691911_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Starbucks Shift Lead – BW Campus",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\n\nLocation: Berea\n\nReports To: Store Manager Employment Type: Full-Time  FLSA Status:  Non-Exempt  Position Summary  A BW Starbucks Shift Lead supports and guides barista teams in delivering excellent customer service, maintaining efficient store operations, and ensuring compliance with health, safety, and security standards. This role oversees daily shift activities, including task delegation, cash handling, and inventory support, while fostering a positive and fast-paced store environment.  This is a full-time, non-exempt position at a Starbucks licensed coffeehouse on the Baldwin Wallace campus. Essential Duties & Responsibilities   Responsibilities may include, but are not limited to, the following:  Operational Leadership: Open/close the store, delegate tasks, and oversee shift operations to ensure service and quality standards are met. Customer Service: Actively resolve customer complaints and ensure a welcoming \"Third Place\" environment. Team Development: Train new employees, coach employees, and provide feedback to the store manager Cash and Inventory Management: Perform cash drops, count registers, and manage food/supply orders. Safety and Standards: Ensure compliance with health, safety, and security guidelines.    Position Requirements  Minimum Qualifications (Education, Skills, Knowledge & Experience) At least one (1) year of experience in retail or food service, demonstrating the ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment; leadership experience is a plus.  At least six (6) months of experience in a position requiring frequent customer interaction.  At least six (6) months of experience delegating tasks to other employees and/or coordinating the work of two (2) or more employees.  Ability to meet store operating policies and standards related to customer service, cash handling, and store safety and security. Ability to prepare and coach the preparation of food and beverages to standard recipes and customized specifications.  Strong interpersonal skills, flexibility, and willingness to learn and build relationships. Preferred Qualifications  Prior successful completion of barista training and certification in beverage preparation standards and commercial beverage equipment operation strongly preferred, or ability to obtain certification within a specified training period. Working Conditions & Physical Requirements  Work is performed in a fast-paced retail environment requiring standing for extended periods and frequent walking, bending, twisting, and reaching. Must be able to lift, carry, and move items weighing up to 25 pounds. Work may involve exposure to confined spaces and high customer traffic. Shifts may include early mornings, evenings, weekends, nights, and holidays. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. Conditions of Employment  Must successfully pass a background check. Successful completion of barista training and certification in beverage preparation standards and commercial beverage equipment operation, or ability to obtain certification within a specified training period.   How to Apply Review of completed applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates should submit a resume via the “To Apply” link on Baldwin Wallace University’s Employment and Careers webpage. We appreciate all applicants; only those selected for an interview will be contacted.  Baldwin Wallace University is an EEO employer and educator. We provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees in accordance with applicable federal, state, and local laws. At BW, we support and encourage diversity in a variety of forms. We value and appreciate inclusive excellence in the classroom, within extracurricular activities and as we engage our community partners.",
      "department": ""
